flowchart TB
  req[Support request]
  ctx[Context from w05 spine<br/>policy rows + order]
  gen[Generator<br/>draft attempt]
  crit[Critic<br/>grades against criteria]
  store[(Policy store<br/>criteria as data)]
  verdict{Verdict}
  rewrite[Optimizer<br/>bounded rewrite]
  cap{Cycles left?}
  ship[Ship reply]
  tele[[Verdict as telemetry<br/>score beside the trace]]

  req --> gen
  ctx --> gen
  gen --> crit
  crit --> store
  store --> crit
  crit --> verdict
  crit --> tele
  verdict -->|pass| ship
  verdict -->|fail| cap
  cap -->|yes, max 1| rewrite
  rewrite --> crit
  cap -->|no| ship

%% ===== AWS deployment view (comment) =====
%% Channel -> AgentCore-hosted generator (Bedrock invoke, draft)
%%   -> Step Functions state machine owns the loop and the cap
%%   -> critic path: Lambda reads the policy row from DynamoDB, then a
%%      second Bedrock invoke returns the JSON verdict
%%   -> Choice state: pass -> ship; fail and under cap -> one rewrite;
%%      at cap -> ship with the violation recorded
%%   -> each verdict written to CloudWatch Omni as an evaluation score
%%      next to the agent trace
%%   -> Bedrock Guardrails filter the final text; they do not grade policy

%% ===== Azure deployment view (comment) =====
%% Channel -> Microsoft Foundry Agent Service (generator agent)
%%   -> Durable Functions orchestrator: deterministic loop, verdict and
%%      iteration count checkpointed in orchestrator history
%%   -> critique activity reads the policy row (Cosmos DB / AI Search),
%%      then a second Foundry model call returns the JSON verdict
%%   -> at the cap the orchestrator ships the rewrite and records the
